    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42955" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσσήν</span></b>  (B), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆνος</span>,
			ὁ, transliteration of Hebr. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>[hudot ]ōšen,</i> worn by Jewish
			priests, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				3.7.5
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3.8.9
			</span></i>, where it is said to mean <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγιον,</span> by which word it is rendered in <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				28.15
			</span></i>.</div>
